authors.bio:
Hi, Im Jiashuo! I'm a fourth-year Ph.D. candidate in the Department of Computer Science & Technology at Tsinghua University, advised by Prof. Peng Cui and Prof. Bo Li. I was a visiting student researcher at Prof. Jose H. Blanchet's group in the Department of Management Science & Engineering at Stanford University. I also work remotely with Prof. Hongseok Namkoong in the Decision, Risk, and Operations division at Columbia Business School. I will visit Prof. Mihaela van der Schaar's group at Cambridge University this summer.

My research lies at the interface of machine learning and operations research, including:
* Generalization under Distribution Shifts: Theoretical foundations and tools for understanding real-world distribution shifts;
* Data Heterogeneity: Algorithms to model and exploit data heterogeneity under distribution shifts;
* Distributionally robust optimization: Addressing the over-pessimism problem in real applications.

Recently, I'm focusing on the evaluation of LLMs as well as incorporating LLMs into robust optimization.

